    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug in the `frai` CLI where the `--ci` flag wasn't being passed through to the `frai-gate` command.\n\n**The Problem:** \nThe `gate` command handler in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` was only passing positional arguments to the `frai-gate` CLI, but commander.js was parsing flags like `--ci` separately (as options) due to `.allowUnknownOption(true)`. These options were never passed through to the delegated CLI.\n\n**The Solution:**\nChanged the action handler to extract all arguments after 'gate' from `process.argv` directly, which includes both positional arguments and all flags. This ensures everything is passed through correctly to `frai-gate`.\n\n**Changes Made:**\n- Modified `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 737-755): Changed the action handler to use `process.argv` instead of relying on commander's argument parsing\n- Rebuilt the package with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n- Verified the fix works: `frai gate init --ci` now correctly creates both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`",
